  "Unpair": "",
  "Unpair connected hearing aids.\nAs Pico-ASHA only supports one set of hearing aids at a time,\nthis allows pairing a different set of hearing aids.": "",
  "USB Settings": "",
  "UAC Version": "",
  "Change USB Audio Class version.\nMost people should stick with UAC2, however UAC1 may be compatible with older operating systems such as Windows XP - 8.\nThis setting will persist, allowing you to set it on one device, then plug it into an older device that only supports UAC1.": "",
  "Min Volume": "",
  "Level at the bottom of the Windows slider (just above mute), in ASHA steps (0.375 dB).\nBelow -127 (-47.6 dB), the hearing aids' floor, the level is\nobtained by digitally attenuating the audio.": "",
  "Max Volume": "",
  "Level at 100% on the Windows slider, in ASHA steps (0.375 dB).": "",
  "Digital Attenuation Below": "",
  "Level (ASHA steps, 0.375 dB) under which the hearing aids' volume stays fixed\nand the audio signal is attenuated digitally instead, like the volume\nslider of a web browser (gives very quiet levels).\n-127 = only below the hearing aids' own floor.\nEqual to Max Volume = fully digital volume (hearing aids' volume never moves).": "",
  "Update": "",
  "AUDIO SETTING EXPERIMENTAL :": "",
  "Experimental: computes Min Volume, Digital Attenuation Below and Max Volume\nfrom the characteristics of the hearing aids.\nA value of 0 leaves the corresponding settings under manual control.": "",
